# Host-only TSan suppressions.
#
# plan9port's libthread lazily initializes per-proc pthread mutexes
# (`lockinit`/`_threadlock`/`chanlock`) while another proc is already
# locking the same global.  TSan reports that initialization as a race even
# though libthread's own locking protocol is what makes it safe.  Keep the
# suppression narrow: o9 actor/channel races should still be reported.
race:*_threadlock*
race:*lockinit*
race:*chanlock*
race:*procmain*
